  "catalog": {
    "slug": "sandwich-shop",
    "title": "Sandwich Shop",
    "version": "0.1.0",
    "author": "simetro",
    "description": "A friendly corner sandwich shop. Slice bread, layer fillings, and ring up hungry customers before the lunch rush turns into a queue out the door.",
    "tags": [
      "sl1",
      "scenario_language_v1",
      "showcase",
      "daily_life",
      "tutorial"
    ],
    "palette_note": "Warm cream and deep teal evoke a bakery countertop; toasted orange for bread, herb green for veggies, mustard for condiments, sky blue for satisfied customers, raspberry for the lunch rush alarm.",
    "layout_note": "Three-place horizontal flow: pantry on the left supplies bread and fillings, the prep counter assembles sandwiches in the middle, the front counter rings them up on the right.",
    "node_language_note": "Place roles: source / compute_cluster (the kitchen) / dashboard (the order counter). One operator overlay for the in-store queue.",
    "mover_path_note": "Movers do not exist yet for SL1 scenes; the legacy pieces.movers array is intentionally empty. SL1 links represent typed dependency between pantry, prep-counter, register, and the manager overlay. Cross-place inventory transport over links lands when the SL1 renderer adopts the link-queue runtime; PR 15a keeps the recipe colocated on prep-counter so the deterministic sandwich pipeline runs inside one place's typed storage.",
    "review_note": "Marked status=draft in the frontend catalog because the SL1 canvas renderer is not yet wired. Selecting this scene loads it successfully and shows catalog metadata in the scene browser. The SL1 HUD chips, dashboard freshness pill, and milestone strip render via the existing SL1 HUD overlay; the bespoke canvas vignette ships when the SL1 renderer is wired in a later PR."
  },
